The rerun preflight now passes and returns `KLEAN_NO_OBLIGATIONS`, zero obligations, and a null target. The initial Lake failure was caused by the command sandbox exposing parent-namespace `/proc` while Lean 4.22 queried its inner PID; a tiny preload shim only corrected `getpid()` for executable discovery. With that environment correction, the trusted checker’s clean build succeeded and the mounted tree remained unchanged.
Producer provenance, all launcher/source/tree hashes, the one-rule canonical inventory, independent classification, and the trusted Stage 4 preflight are complete. Proof-mode work is inapplicable because the launcher mode is CLASSIFICATION_ONLY and /candidate is absent.
